      "q": "9. A series LCR circuit with $R=20\\Omega $, $L=1.5H$ and $C=35\\mu F$ is connected to a variable frequency $200V$ ac supply. When the frequency of the supply equals the natural frequency of the circuit, what is the average power transferred to the circuit in one complete cycle?",
      "a": "It is known that,\nResistance, $R=20\\Omega $\nInductance, $L=1.5H$\nCapacitance, $C=35\\mu F=35\\times {{10}^{-6}}F$\nVoltage, $V=200V$\nIt is known that,\nImpedance,$Z=\\sqrt{{{R}^{2}}+{{({{X}_{L}}-{{X}_{C}})}^{2}}}$\nAt resonance, ${{X}_{L}}={{X}_{C}}$\n$\\Rightarrow Z=R=20\\Omega $\n$I=\\frac{V}{Z}=\\frac{200}{20}$\n$\\Rightarrow I=10A$\nAverage power, $P={{I}^{2}}R$\n$\\Rightarrow P={{10}^{2}}\\times 20$\n$\\Rightarrow P=2000W$\nTherefore, the average power transferred is $2000W$."
