      "a": "The slope of the cut-off voltage (V) versus frequency (\u03bd) of an incident light is given as: V/v = 4.12\u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u2075 Vs V is related to frequency by the equation hv = eV Where, e = Charge on an electron = 1.6 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u2079 C and h = Planck\u2019s constant Therefore, h = e \u00d7 V/v = 1.6\u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u2079 \u00d7 4.12 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b9\u2075 = 6.592 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\u2074 Js Hence, the value of Plank\u2019s constant is 6.592 \u00d7 10\u207b\u00b3\u2074 Js."
